// "Go harder" investigation (see dev-journal/2026-08-17-map-fold-thermite-limits.md):
// the NATURAL, obviously-correct implementation of a resolver-style
// assert-into-log operation. Expected: `forge check` FAILS with
// "postcondition not satisfied" on the frame-property ens (line 3) --
// not because the implementation is wrong, but because
// TMapU64Bool::insert's own generated Verus postcondition
// (thermite-lower/src/lower.rs:5499) only promises the NEW key's
// presence and len+1, nothing about any other key's membership being
// preserved. A caller has no fact to prove the frame property from,
// through Map's current surface API.

fn apply_assert(asserted: Map<u64, bool>, new_fact: u64, other_fact: u64) -> Map<u64, bool>
  req !asserted.contains_key(new_fact) && asserted.len() < 1_000_000 && other_fact != new_fact
  ens result.contains_key(new_fact)
  ens result.contains_key(other_fact) == asserted.contains_key(other_fact)
  ens result.len() == asserted.len() + 1
  fx  alloc
{
  let mut result = asserted;
  result.insert(new_fact, true);
  result
}
